// City-specific SEO intro copy for prerendered city home pages.
//
// Each entry keyed by "{country}-{city}" provides a short bilingual paragraph
// describing the city's distinct character and coverage areas. This content is
// injected into the prerendered <div id="root"> body so non-JS crawlers
// (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, Googlebot) can distinguish same-country city pages from
// one another — a requirement of the check-city-similarity CI gate (80%
// Jaccard threshold). Strings here are per-city descriptive copy, not UI
// strings that pass through the React i18n system.
//
// Rules for new entries:
//   • Include 4-5 neighbourhood or village names specific to THAT city.
//   • Avoid reusing place names that appear in another entry for the same
//     country — each word token must be unique to the city to widen Jaccard
//     distance.
//   • Provide EN, AR, and FR versions; the CI check runs EN only but all three
//     languages are served to international crawlers.

// i18n-ignore — city-specific crawler-facing descriptive copy; not rendered in the client UI

